I looked at this again and found that IPC Phase 5 demands strict quantitative measures along with triggering three metrics simultaneously;

* Food consumption&#x20;
  &#x20;At least 20% households facing total lack of food or catastrophe.
* Malnutrition Criterion
  &#x20;Global acute malnutrition exceeding 30%.
* Mortality criterion&#x20;
  &#x20;Death rate exceeding 2 deaths per 10,000 people per day.&#x20;

Establishing a formal Famine classification requires a verification of the data and conditions on the ground and in the midst of war and sieges along with internet blockades it's a monumental task for the humanitarian teams to conduct a survey.

I looked at the available data to substantiate the case for Famine in Sudan and almost all three criteria that I've mentioned above met it or exceeded it.&#x20;

